&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.climate.columbia.edu/" target="_blank"&gt;Columbia Climate School&lt;/a&gt;, the&lt;a href="https://www.climatefilmfest.com/" target="_blank"&gt; Climate Film Festival&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href="https://www.momscleanairforce.org/" target="_blank"&gt;Moms Clean Air Force&lt;/a&gt; are co-hosting an Earth Month screening of The Plastic Detox (2026, dir. Josh Murphy and Louie Psihoyos), followed by a post-screening discussion exploring the film&amp;rsquo;s themes around plastic pollution, its connections to climate change, and the broader environmental impacts of plastics. This free event will be open to the public with advance RSVP.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
